    "fullText": "physical, mental and even spiritual phases of a natural life are The main trouble with the average individuals of present-day civilization is that they refuse to think.  They prefer \"mob thinking. \" Because everybody else does it, it must be right!  The real facts prove the opposite to be the case.  The genuine principles of healing are simple and few; in fact, so simple that the so-called scientific mind is prone to overlook the vital points of the application of the law.  Youth, strength and happiness need not belong to the young in years alone, for the young in desire and creative energy, may also have these much-to-be-desired possessions.  Never permit yourself to lose sight of the fact that while there is a spark of life in your bodies it can be formed into an intense flame.  For strength is born of desire.  Professor Ehret recognizes a number of causes that produce dis. ease besides \"mucus\" although this word is used in the title.  Non-mucusforming foods are dearly defined, and the student can be guided accordingly."
