    "fullText": "cult for the Cure and Prevention of Disease known. I have no Some days I felt well and on others felt very bad, so I soon went back home, returning to the so-called \"good eating,\" as lived and suggested by well-meaning friends, relatives and physicians.  I had learned something about fasting, but it was opposed by all friends and relatives; even my former naturopathic doctor told my sister that to a person with Bright's disease a few days' fast would prove fatal.  { 14] The next winter I went to Algiers, in northern Africa.  The mild climate and the wonderful fruits improved my condition and gave me more faith in Nature's methods and an understanding of them, and I gained courage to try short fasts to assist the cleansing properties of fruit and climate, with such results that one morning of a well feeling day I chanced to notice in my mirror that my face had taken on an entirely new look; that of a younger and healthy looking person."
