    "fullText": "one, I could not take up again what I firmly believed and had On the eighteenth day my young friend became quite hoarse, and fearing he would lose his voicenot then knowing what caused itended his fast with about three pounds of figs, at my suggestion, with the result that for nearly an hour he raised a very large quantity of mucus from his throat and his body cleansed itself in other directions.  His voice soon being restored and his stuttering disappeared and has never returned.  We had accomplished what his rich father had in vain tried to do by employing almost every known treatment for him, without the slightest permanent improvement.  Fasting, Nature's Supreme Remedy, has been so crudely practiced, and is so generally misunderstood, that it is very important that it be rightly explained."
