    "fullText": "that I desired to perfect and verify the methods employed, so I In Egypt, we saw a race of people of extraordinary strength and endurance, living on a scanty vegetarian diet mosrly, but with two supposedly bad habits - cigarette smoking and drinking strong coffee; yet we saw not a single nervous or toxemic person.  To see how few kinds and how little food they ate, to learn that they are about the same kinds of foods that their ancestors ate, gives one a reason for the superior qualities of old Egyptian civilization.  In Palestine we stayed several months, studying local customs, records and history of past conditions, with the result that my conception of the real meaning of the New Testament gospels was changed very much."
