    "excerpt": "Bladder Your bladder is mainly a holding, collecting tank, or sac, for urine on its way out from the kidneys.  The elimination of urine from the bladder is called “micturition,” “voiding” or “urination. ” Urethra The tube that leads from the bladder to the outside of your body.",
    "fullText": "Urinary System Bladder Your bladder is mainly a holding, collecting tank, or sac, for urine on its way out from the kidneys.  The elimination of urine from the bladder is called “micturition,” “voiding” or “urination. ” Urethra The tube that leads from the bladder to the outside of your body."
