    "excerpt": "The pharynx is a muscular tube that connects the nasal cavity to the larynx. It also connects the mouth with the esophagus. It extends from the base of your skull to your sixth cervical vertebra. There it divides into anterior (behind), which becomes the esophagus, and inferior (in front), which becomes the larynx.",
    "fullText": "Pharynx The pharynx is a muscular tube that connects the nasal cavity to the larynx. It also connects the mouth with the esophagus. It extends from the base of your skull to your sixth cervical vertebra. There it divides into anterior (behind), which becomes the esophagus, and inferior (in front), which becomes the larynx."
