    "excerpt": "4.  Fatty acids and glycerol bind to form neutral fats, which then bond to various proteins to form chylomicrons.  Fats in this form are absorbed and carried throughout the lymphatic system and the blood system where they are dispersed to the tissues of the body.  Fatty acids cannot be converted to glucose.  However, t...",
    "fullText": "An Example Of Fat Metabolism 4.  Fatty acids and glycerol bind to form neutral fats, which then bond to various proteins to form chylomicrons.  Fats in this form are absorbed and carried throughout the lymphatic system and the blood system where they are dispersed to the tissues of the body.  Fatty acids cannot be converted to glucose.  However, they can enter the Krebs (energy) Cycle through acetyl groups.  5.  Adipose (fatty) tissue is created for the body’s energy reserve and factors for cellular health and immunity."
