    "fullText": "The Energy Of Meat ) As we begin to pass our adrenal weaknesses down genetically, future generations may see multiple sclerosis, Parkinson’s, Addison’s Disease, and other neurological weaknesses develop from a chronic lack of neurotransmitters.  High blood pressure can also be a result of adrenal gland weakness.  When the adrenal glands become weak, we also begin to fail at producing adequate steroids (our anti-inflam-matories), because meat is highly acidforming (which creates inflammation).  The body will use cholesterol in place of steroids where this inflammation is present.  This becomes a serious problem because lipids, in the presence of aci-dosis, stick together and plaque themselves “in” and “onto” tissues.  Energy from eating meat can also come from growth hormones fed to the cattle (or other animals) for rapid growth.  Energy should be dynamic or cellular, not created by stimulants."
