    "excerpt": "Vaccinations: The Poison Needles “Like treats like” is a concept used by the allopathic (medical) and homeopathic (more natural) modalities to treat diseases.  Along this line, one of the most toxic and oftentimes fatal concepts and practices that science has created is that of inoculation or “vaccinations,” whereby li...",
    "fullText": "Module 4.4 Vaccinations: The Poison Needles “Like treats like” is a concept used by the allopathic (medical) and homeopathic (more natural) modalities to treat diseases.  Along this line, one of the most toxic and oftentimes fatal concepts and practices that science has created is that of inoculation or “vaccinations,” whereby live parasites are injected into the body, hoping the body will develop an immunity to them.  The reason for this is that parasites (germs) are considered to be the cause of most diseases.  Today, science is slowly moving away from this idea, replacing it with the concept of genetics or genes being the “bad boys. ” An excellent example of the “like treats like” fallacy is the polio vaccine.  The theory is: To build your immunity to this virus, simply take in more of the same virus, but in smaller dosages."
