    "fullText": "Toxic Chemicals A large number of the above-cited pesticides, herbicides, fungicides, petrochemicals, etc. , are hormone disrupters.  They inhibit or stimulate the production of hormones or steroids, like estrogen and testosterone.  Benzene levels in air, water and food have skyrocketed.  Benzene is a known carcinogen, which is used in solvents and food additives, and emitted from oil refineries, gas stations, rubber (tire) manufacturing plants and diesel powered vehicles.  An astronomical amount of carcinogenic substances are released into our air and our water from tobacco smoke, gas and especially diesel emissions, body shops, airports, highways, railways, subways, most industries, boating, petro-production plants, etc.  Radiation is another high source of our cancers."
