    "excerpt": "The body digests, absorbs, utilizes, reproduces, and eliminates in the presence of fluids.  These fluids include digestive juices, blood, extra- and intra-cellular fluids, lymphatic fluids and urine.  To fully understand the effects that food and toxins have within your body, however, you first have to understand oppos...",
    "fullText": "Third Root: Overacidity—Acidosis The body digests, absorbs, utilizes, reproduces, and eliminates in the presence of fluids.  These fluids include digestive juices, blood, extra- and intra-cellular fluids, lymphatic fluids and urine.  To fully understand the effects that food and toxins have within your body, however, you first have to understand opposites.  Creation exists because of the dynamic interplay of opposites, without which everything would be the same.  (Of course, because God is One, the closer to God you get, the more the opposites merge. ) The interplay between opposites creates movement, activity, shapes, sizes, colors, temperatures.  As complicated as chemistry is, it rests upon two pillars or opposites: hot and cold, or yin and yang, the names for the two opposing dynamics within Chinese philosophy and medicine.  Hot is called acid and cold is alkaline.  Acids initiate change and alkalis balance.  This is the basis of all matter."
