    "fullText": "Module 5.5 This happens the same way that you, in every moment, express yourself according to the experiences you have and the memory of these experiences.  Your cells are no different.  With each minute, hour, day … the strength or weakness of each of your cells becomes a part of its memory patterns in DNA and chromosomes.  At the moment of conception the condition of each cell and its memories that are passed down to you become a part of your body, and thus determine how your body functions and the conditions that it can experience.  Since we keep making our genetic condition weaker by continuing to wear down our bodies through diet and lifestyle we are seeing a landslide of chronic cellular and tissue weaknesses.  We then pass them on to our children, who then pass them on to their children.  And with each successive generation, the cellular patterns and functions become more chronic, causing disease symptoms to appear now in infants."
