    "fullText": "Module 8.2 False Unicorn (Helonias) One of nature’s top tonics, especially for the male and female reproductive organs and glands.  Strengthens the endocrine glands.  Use in prolapsed conditions of the intestines, uterus, hemorrhoids, veins, etc.  It revitalizes and regenerates tissue, especially the reproductive tissues.  Increases the ability of conception.  Strengthens the mucous membranes, especially the genital-urinary tissues.  Use for diabetes.  Use for ovarian, uterine or prostate weakness or conditions.  Helps prevent miscarriages.  Use for sterility problems.  Use for relaxed vagina.  Scientific name: Chamaelirium luteum Parts used: Root and rhizomes.  Actions: Anthelmintic (vermifuge), cellular proliferant, diuretic, emetic (high doses), emmenagogue, oxytocic, sialagogue (fresh), stimulating, tonic, uterine tonic.  Fenugreek Fenugreek is a great expectorant.  It softens, loosens, and helps expel mucus (phlegm), especially from the bronchial and lung tissues."
