    "fullText": "Module 8.2 Shown to kill various fungi and bacteria including: staphylococcus, streptococcus, chlamydia, salmonella typhi, corynebacterium, vibrio cholerae, trichomonas vaginalis, shigella, giardia, treponema pallidum, pseudomonas, pneumococcus, and candida albicans.  Has some larger parasitic activity as well.  Also used against protozoas.  A nerve tonic.  Slightly laxative.  Scientific name: Mohonia spp.  Parts used: Root and rhizome.  Actions: Alterative, antiperiodic, antiscorbutic, anti-scrofulous, antisyphilitic, depurant, diuretic, hepatic, laxative, nerve tonic, stimulant (slightly), tonic.  Parsley A tremendous herb for the urinary tract and adrenal glands.  Has a strengthening and cleansing effect upon the bladder and kidneys.  High in chlorophyll, therefore it enhances the blood and cleans and moves the lymphatics.  Excellent for heavy metal and chemical toxicity.  Enhances nerve and heart function.  Superb for the endocrine glands.  Increases the iron-carrying capacity of the blood."
