    "fullText": "Appendix G includes digestive and all the processes used to break down complex substances into simple, usable ones; 3.  Energy is generally released during this process.  (For example: glucose is catabolized to water, carbon dioxide, and energy. ) Cataplasm another name for a poultice.  Catarrh a mucus discharge from the mucous membranes as a result of inflammation, acids, or irritants (foreign proteins).  This has special reference to the air passages of the head and throat.  (For example: hayfever, rhinitis, influenza, bronchitis, pharyngitis, asthma).  Milk and refined sugars create an over-production of mucus discharge, congesting various body tissues.  Cathartic strong laxative which causes rapid evacuation of bowels (Black Hellebore, Culvers Root, Senna Leaves).  Cationic 1.  state of flux and breakdown whereby nutrients and elements are dispersed systemically; similar to catabolic; 3.  in reference to alkalization."
