    "fullText": "Appendix G Desiccants herbs that are able to dry surfaces by absorbing moisture (Agar Agar, Bladderwrack Powder, Corn Starch, Marshmallow, Slippery Elm Powder).  Detergent cleansing to wounds, ulcers or skin itself (Amaranth plant, Bitter Root, Poke Root).  Detoxicant removes toxins.  Detoxification the process of cleansing and alkalizing the body.  The removing of obstructions (e. g. , acids, mucus, parasites, chemicals, minerals, metals, thoughts and emotions) that block energy and the proper function of cells and the individual.  A necessary requirement in returning to vibrant health.  Detoxify 1.  to remove the toxic quality of a substance; 2.  treatment of a toxic overdose of any medicine but especially of the toxic state produced by drugs of abuse or acute alcoholism.  Diaphoretic causes perspiration and increases elimination through the skin (Centaury, Coltsfoot, Sassafras).  Diastolic the second (or bottom) number in a blood pressure reading."
