    "fullText": "Appendix G More than 100 have been identified.  Elements found in the human body include oxygen, aluminum, carbon, cobalt, hydrogen, nitrogen, calcium, phosphorus, potassium, sulfur, sodium, chlorine, magnesium, iron, fluorine, iodine, copper, manganese, and zinc.  Emetic induces vomiting (Black Mustard, Blood Root, Mistletoe).  Emmenagogue helps promote and regulate menstruation (Saw Palmetto, False Unicorn, Nettle).  Emollient soothes, softens and protects the skin, or soothes the irritated mucosa.  Emulsion a combination of two liquids that do not mix with each other, such as oil and water; one substance is broken into tiny droplets and is suspended within the other.  Emulsification is the first step in the digestion of fats.  Enervate to deprive of strength, vigor, etc. ; to weaken physically and mentally.  Endocrine System the system of glands that secrete hormones, steroids, and neurotransmitters directly into the bloodstream."
