    "excerpt": "With a cluster of sparks, The air of'rudition, That which is nourished, Will come to fruition. Vision — the power, It molds and makes. Hold it true so long And evermore it shapes, The reasons, minds, and the wills Calling forth a thousand joys, Disposing of a thousand ills. Cherished in secret Yet coming to pass, Visio...",
    "fullText": "C O A L S With a cluster of sparks, The air of'rudition, That which is nourished, Will come to fruition. Vision — the power, It molds and makes. Hold it true so long And evermore it shapes, The reasons, minds, and the wills Calling forth a thousand joys, Disposing of a thousand ills. Cherished in secret Yet coming to pass, Vision — the calm In a pool of glass. Tempest tossed souls, Wherever you be, Rest under the wing Of the visionary. In the Ocean of Life, Isles of Bliss lay smiling. The Sunny shore of your ideal Awaits your arriving. Keep your hand firmly poised Upon the helm of thought. Hold true to the vision And you'll find what you have sought. T H E V I S I O N A R Y ' S"
