    "fullText": "E X P L A I N When she announced that some young chimpanzees in the group killed 4 monkeys, one antelope, and a pig, we saluted this as a scientific contribution.  Alas, it was only a deviation due to what our civilization reflected on the chimpanzees. '\" The point here is instructive.  Many chimpanzee groups - especially the bonobo chimps (the most genetically similar to humans) - do not engage in hunting behavior."
