    "excerpt": "Brian Clement, director of the Hippocrates Health Institute, is a blood type 0 and has been a vegetarian for over 40 years.  Dr.  Gabriel Cousens is a blood type 0 and has been a raw-food vegetarian for over 20 years.  There are hundreds of other examples I could site.  In my own experience in counseling people on diet...",
    "fullText": "O R I G I N S Brian Clement, director of the Hippocrates Health Institute, is a blood type 0 and has been a vegetarian for over 40 years.  Dr.  Gabriel Cousens is a blood type 0 and has been a raw-food vegetarian for over 20 years.  There are hundreds of other examples I could site.  In my own experience in counseling people on diet, I have found the suggestions of what foods are agreeable and disagreeable based on one's blood type to be often applicable to cooked foods and rarely applicable to raw foods and raw- food eaters."
