    "fullText": "O R I G I N S I eating wild game and fish, worms and insects of all types, as well as eggs.  Such raw animal-food diets are promoted without any mention of restrictions or parameters of quantity.  \"Instinktive eating\" is one such philosophy as promoted by the staunch evolutionist Frenchman, Guy Claude-Burger, Eating raw animal flesh is better than cooked animal flesh for a time and people will feel better until the body begins to accumulate the stronger, unmiti- gated death energy (karma) of the animals in the raw state.  This is why primitive tribes usually ate mostly cooked animal foods and did so with respect and understanding of the cycle of karma, life and death.  I have seen people on high-concentration, raw animal-food diets over the long term and have seen lives significantly altered by the negative energy of such foods."
