    "fullText": "O R I G I N S I personally believe, based on my experience, that eating a diet consisting of 10% or more raw animal flesh leads to or exacerbates major phys- ical, psycho-social issues including: addictive behavior, emotional imbalances, body odor, cancer, immobility, infertility, and parasite challenges.  It is interesting to note that wild chimpanzees, who include animal food in their diet (mostly insects), do not exceed 10% animal food in their nutrition.  Unchecked levels of raw animal-food consumption seems to be associated with a poverty consciousness - a subconscious belief that killing, lack and hard- ship are laws of life.  Repeatedly thinking about demineralized food and deficiency is another facet of a poverty mentality.  Thoughts of lack create lack.  Thoughts of abundance create abundance.  Feelings of fear along with thoughts of lack, deficiency, and doubt lead one to create a reality and diet where those thoughts thrive."
