    "fullText": "T H E Secret Revealed Interestingly, protein can be adequately supplied by raw plant foods.  Animal protein is not necessary to meet protein needs.  The consumption of cooked animal protein has been statistically correlated with all the major diseases of civilization.  As the cooked animal protein increases in the diet, the rate of disease increases in a one-to-one correlation (for more on this see John Robbins' book Diet For A New America and Howard Lyman's book Mad Cowboy)."
