    "excerpt": "You will also notice that these fruits corre- spond to what is available in the fall and winter.  Sulfur-residue foods warm the body.  Sulfur-residue foods include: cruciferous vegetables, garlic, and onions.  Durian has a high sulfur and potassium-yield.  In Asia, one who overeats durian is often said to have \"hot eye...",
    "fullText": "U S E T H E You will also notice that these fruits corre- spond to what is available in the fall and winter.  Sulfur-residue foods warm the body.  Sulfur-residue foods include: cruciferous vegetables, garlic, and onions.  Durian has a high sulfur and potassium-yield.  In Asia, one who overeats durian is often said to have \"hot eyes. \" H o w TO USE T H E S U N F O O D TRIANGLE Eat a meal that is high in fats, potassium, and/or sulfur and you will notice a heating reaction within 45 minutes as the food begins to digest.  This reaction will become more pronounced over time as one becomes more purified by eating a raw-food diet.  Eating To Cool The Body \" T H E L I F E F O R C E F L O W S T H R O U G H T H E B O D Y , A N D B Y A C T I N G O N T H E R E S I S T A N C E O F F E R E D B Y F O O D , G E N E R A T E S H E A T A N D E N E R G Y AS A B Y - P R O D U C T .  \" — Dugald Semple, The Sunfood Way To Health We can do five things to cool the body nutritionally: 1.  Fast."
