    "excerpt": "The Sun evaporates water from the leaves of plants, concentrating the proto- plasm solution.  Thus, due to osmosis (the movement of water from an area of greater concentration to an area of lesser concentration), water containing soluble minerals is spirally suctioned up from the roots into the leaves of the plant.  In...",
    "fullText": "M I N E R A L T R A D E - O U T The Sun evaporates water from the leaves of plants, concentrating the proto- plasm solution.  Thus, due to osmosis (the movement of water from an area of greater concentration to an area of lesser concentration), water containing soluble minerals is spirally suctioned up from the roots into the leaves of the plant.  In this way the protoplasm is continuously concentrated and the leaves become loaded with colloidal minerals suspended with Sun and Earth energies.  Each plant mines a different spectrum of minerals from the soil and provides a different nutrition to the body."
