    "fullText": "M I N E R A L Trade—Out This is when the teeth problems arise, which is indicative of the body purging acids and also indicative of a lack of minerals in the body and diet, especially calcium, magnesium, iron and silicon.  At the point of mineral trade-out, one needs to take in at least 2. 5 pounds (1. 1 kg) of green-leafed vegetables daily (one-third eaten, two-thirds juiced), increase the intake of sea vegetables, use up to ten tablespoons of green super- foods (powdered grasses and algae) per day, include more seeds to help synergize and utilize the green foods and simultaneously cut down on eating hybridized sweet fruit and high-fat, acid-forming nuts.  mineral.  Interestingly, calcium also makes up about 50% ot the alkaline earth mineral matter of the human body, and is found in all bodily tissues, but chiefly in the bones, teeth and the muscles.  The importance of leaf minerals for the human body cannot be overstated."
