    "fullText": "T H E A L L R A W Diet Weekly M E N U An increase in caloric needs is also determined by physical exercise.  For example, a 165-pound (74. 3 kg) male may need 2,970 calories for a normal day's routine.  However, if the same man engages in vigorous activity throughout the day, caloric needs may double, up to 5,940 calories.  As an example, a caloric sample of the foods from the diet plans is provided."
