    "excerpt": "An alkaloid in abuta, tetrandrine, has been documented to have various actions on heart function in animals and humans.  Those with a heart condition or taking heart medications should consult with their doctor before using this plant.  2.  Abuta has demonstrated to be a uterine relaxant and traditionally employed as a...",
    "fullText": "1. Abuta (*Cissampelos pareira*) An alkaloid in abuta, tetrandrine, has been documented to have various actions on heart function in animals and humans.  Those with a heart condition or taking heart medications should consult with their doctor before using this plant.  2.  Abuta has demonstrated to be a uterine relaxant and traditionally employed as a childbirth aid.  A pregnant woman should use it only under the supervision of a qualified healthcare practitioner.  3.  In studies with mice, abuta extracts have demonstrated female anti-fertility activity by modulating the hormones specifically responsible for fertility.  Those seeking to get pregnant should avoid the use of abuta.  - **Note Vitaliste** : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr.  Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne."
