    "fullText": "4. Achocha (*Cyclanthera pedata*) htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Caigua seeds contain 28-30 amino acids as well as a group of trypsin inhibitors  - Two of these  - chrysin-6-C-fucopyranoside and apigenin-6-C-glucopyranoside (isovitexin)  - were found to be the main constituents in both the leaves and fruits of caigua  - In addition  - the fruits have yielded nine triterpenoid saponins  - among them six new natural compounds never seen before  - The seeds have been reported with six new cucurbitacin glycosides - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - In herbal medicine systems in Peru  - The fruits are boiled in milk and gargled for tonsilitis  - The fruit juice is also recommended for high cholesterol  - hypertension  - tonsilitis  - arteriosclerosis - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1.  **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs.  2."
