    "fullText": "6. Ajos Sacha (*Pseudocalymma alliaceum*) **Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel** : Ajos sacha is well used and respected by most of the indigenous Indian tribes of the Amazon and almost all parts of the plant are used; the leaves, vine bark, and root.  Most consider the plant to be “magical” or “spiritual” and capable of driving away evil spirits or used for good luck.  The leaves, tied in bunches, can often be found in local huts ...  - **Posologie & Modes d'Administration** :  - **Dosage Standard** : relieves pain kills bacteria Leaf or Bark reduces inflammation kills fungi Decoction: 1 cup 2-3 times daily fights free radicals kills head lice Tincture: 3-4 ml twice daily relieves oxidative stress kills parasites Capsules: 1-2 g twice daily reduces fever protects heart eases colds & flu prevents atherosclerosis kills viruses reduces spasms lowers blood pressure protects cells & organs  - **Infusion / Décoction** : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min."
