    "fullText": "11. Andiroba (*Carapa guianensis*) **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs.  2.  **Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : Andiroba oil has demonstrated broad spectrum pharmacological activities in clinical research.  The oil extracted from its seeds has antimicrobial effects against Staphylococcus aureus, Escherichia coli and Candida albicans.  Its bioactive compounds, such as limonoids and fatty acids, have demonstrated anti-inflammatory properties, speeding up wound healing and relieving pain, particularly in cases s...  3.  **Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel** : The indigenous peoples in the Amazon have used andiroba in many ways for centuries, and virtually all parts of the tree, as well as the seed oil are utilized.  The Munduruku Indians traditionally used the oil for the mummification of human heads taken as war trophies.  The Wayapi, Palikur, and Creole Indian tribes have used andiroba oil to remove tic..."
