    "fullText": "13. Aveloz (*Euphorbia insulana*) The root is used for snakebite; the latex is used for skin tumors and syphilis ulcers; the seeds and latex are used for intestinal parasites; and decoctions of the wood are used for bacterial infections.  In Malaysia, the stems are pounded and applied to swellings, and in the Dutch Indies, the po...  - **Posologie & Modes d'Administration** :  - **Dosage Standard** : promotes tumors mildly laxative Latex causes cancer Not recommended immune suppressant causes vomiting irritates membranes activates viruses  - **Infusion / Décoction** : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.   - **Teinture** : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour.  - **Contre-indications & Précautions** :  - The latex is considered a poison and has caused deaths in Africa.  Contact of the latex with the eyes can cause blindness.  The caustic latex can also cause skin burns, ulcerations, and dermatitis."
