    "fullText": "16. Bitter Melon (*Momordica charantia*) htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Bitter melon contains an array of biologically active plant chemicals  - The major chemical constituents are cucurbitane type triterpenoids  - cucurbitane type triterpene glycosides  - polyphenols  - essential oils  - fatty acids  - amino acids  - sterols and saponins constituents and some proteins - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - In the Amazon  - Medicinally  - A leaf tea is used for diabetes  - to expel intestinal gas  - to promote menstruation  - and as an antiviral for measles - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1.  **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs.  2.  **Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : Bitter melon has been the subject of a huge amount of research – more than 1,500 studies published on this important rainforest medicinal plant!"
