    "fullText": "18. Boldo (*Peumus boldus*) - **Famille Botanique** :  - **Noms Usuels / Synonymes** : Boldo - **Parties Utilisées** : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - **Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme** : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - **Source Primaire Rain-Tree** : [Boldo Monograph on Rain-Tree. com](https://www. rain-tree. com/boldo. htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Boldo has many biologically active chemicals  - At least 17 alkaloids have been documented thus far  - several of which are believed to be boldo's main active constituents  - In various studies over the years boldine has shown to protect the liver  - to stimulate the production of bile in the liver  - as well as to stimulate digestion  - In other laboratory tests  - boldine has demonstrated diuretic - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - Chemicals in boldo may thin the blood  - chronic use  - Do not exceed the recommended dosages - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1."
