    "fullText": "31. Carqueja (*Baccharis genistelloides*) - **Famille Botanique** :  - **Noms Usuels / Synonymes** : Carqueja - **Parties Utilisées** : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - **Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme** : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - **Source Primaire Rain-Tree** : [Carqueja Monograph on Rain-Tree. com](https://www. rain-tree. com/carqueja. htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Carqueja is a rich source of flavonoids  - which are a type of polyphenol  - Certain flavonoids  - such as silymarin in milk thistle  - Carqueja is rather like a South American version of milk thistle  - It contains up to 20% flavonoids  - including quercetin  - luteolin - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - Carqueja should not be used during pregnancy  - As such  - it is contraindicated in persons with hypoglycemia - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1."
