    "fullText": "39. Cipo Cabeludo (*Mikania hirsutissima*) Chronic long-term use of any diuretic can cause electrolyte and mineral imbalances as well as other medical problems and are generally not recommended; therefore, it is probably best to avoid chronic use of this plant.  2.  While not substantiated scientifically, it is possible that cipo cabeludo may demonstrate a blood thinning effect due to its coumarin content.  Consult your doctor before using this plant if you are taking coumadin drugs (or if coumadin anticoagulant-type drugs are contraindicated for your condition).  - **Note Vitaliste** : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr.  Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne."
