    "fullText": "43. Condurango (*Marsdenia cundurango*) htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Condurango contains a group of novel glycosides and steroids  - patents on these novel compounds as anti-tumor substances in the 1980s  - However  - since filing these patents  - Other constituents in condurango include hydroxylated pregnane derivatives  - chlorogenic and caffeic acids  - as well as various cyclitols  - flavonoids - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - It is also used to relieve nausea and vomiting  - to calm nervous stomachs  - to relieve stomach pain and cramps  - for gastric ulcers  - and to increase bile in the gallbladder  - liver and pancreas - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1.  **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs.  2.  **Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : Condurango has been reported with anti-inflammatory and antioxidant actions in animal studies."
