    "excerpt": "Persons with diabetes and hypoglycemia should use this plant with caution, as blood sugar levels should be monitored accordingly for this possible effect.  Damiana has a traditional use as an abortive and is contraindicated during pregnancy.  2.  **Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : Only one clinical study ha...",
    "fullText": "52. Damiana (*Turnera aphrodisiaca*) Persons with diabetes and hypoglycemia should use this plant with caution, as blood sugar levels should be monitored accordingly for this possible effect.  Damiana has a traditional use as an abortive and is contraindicated during pregnancy.  2.  **Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : Only one clinical study has been conducted to validate the traditional use of the plant for sexual dysfunction and impotence.  In 1999, a group of researchers in Italy administered damiana to both sexually potent and sexually sluggish (or impotent) rats.  The extract had no effect on sexually potent rats but, in the others, it increased the percentage of rats achieving ejaculation and made them more...  3.  **Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel** : Damiana was recorded to be used as an aphrodisiac in the ancient Mayan civilization, as well as for \"giddiness and loss of balance."
