    "fullText": "53. Embauba (*Cecropia peltata, palmata*) - **Famille Botanique** :  - **Noms Usuels / Synonymes** : Embauba - **Parties Utilisées** : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - **Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme** : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - **Source Primaire Rain-Tree** : [Embauba Monograph on Rain-Tree. com](https://www. rain-tree. com/cecropia. htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Embauba is known to contain glycosides  - lipids  - alkaloids  - tannins  - cardenolids  - triterpenes  - polyphenols  - steroids - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - It should not be taken during pregnancy  - increasing the strength of cardiac muscle contraction  - Embauba has demonstrated a hypoglycemic effect in animals  - It is contraindicated for persons with hypoglycemia - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1.  **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : 1.  Embauba has a traditional use of aiding childbirth and to promote menstruation.  It should not be taken during pregnancy."
