    "excerpt": "Gervâo has been used in herbal medicine as an abortive agent and, therefore, is probably contraindicated during pregnancy.  2.  Gervâo has been documented with vasodilator properties in a animal study and, therefore, may lower blood pressure.  Those with low blood pressure or those on antihypertensive medications shoul...",
    "fullText": "59. Gerv&atilde;o (*Stachytarpheta jamaicensis*) Gervâo has been used in herbal medicine as an abortive agent and, therefore, is probably contraindicated during pregnancy.  2.  Gervâo has been documented with vasodilator properties in a animal study and, therefore, may lower blood pressure.  Those with low blood pressure or those on antihypertensive medications should consult their doctor before using gervâo.  3.  Stachytarpheta cayennensis (but not S.  jamaicensis ) has been reported to contain a small amount of naturally-occurring salicylic acid.  This phytochemical is the natural precursor to aspirin.  Those allergic to aspirin should probably avoid using this plant product.  - **Note Vitaliste** : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr.  Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne."
