    "fullText": "60. Graviola (*Annona muricata*) htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Many active compounds and chemicals have been found in graviola  - as scientists have been studying its properties since the 1940s  - Graviola produces these natural compounds in its leaf and stem  - bark  - fruit and fruit seeds  - These chemicals in general have been documented with antitumorous  - antiparasitic  - insecticidal - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - Graviola has demonstrated hypotensive  - vasodilator  - Chronic  - Large single dosages may cause nausea or vomiting  - Reduce the usage accordingly if this occurs  - norepinephrine  - and monomine oxidase activity  - however - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1.  **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : 1.  Graviola has demonstrated uterine stimulant activity in an animal study (rats) and should therefore not be used during pregnancy.  2."
