    "fullText": "62. Guaco (*Mikania guaco*) In large dosages (two to three times the traditional remedy above) guaco has been reported to cause nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea.  2.  Guaco contains a significant amount of coumarin which is the plant chemical coumadin drugs are derived from.  Coumarin has an anti-coagulant and blood thinning effect and the use of guaco may demonstrate anticoagulant effects due to the coumarin content.  Consult with your physician before taking this plant if you are taking coumadin drugs or if coumadin anticoagulant type drugs are contraindicated for your condition."
