    "fullText": "65. Guarana (*Paullinia cupana*) htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - He isolated a bitter  - white crystalline substance with a remarkable physiological action  - Von Martius named this substance guaranine  - and it was later renamed caffeine  - Many today still believe guaranine to be a unique phytochemical in guaraná  - It is  - however (according to chemists)  - caffeine - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - Not to be used during pregnancy or while breast-feeding  - cardiac disorders  - diabetes  - ulcers  - epilepsy  - and other disorders - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1.  **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : 1.  Not to be used during pregnancy or while breast-feeding.  2.  Guaraná contains caffeine and should not be used by those who are sensitive or allergic to caffeine or xanthines.  Excessive consumption of caffeine is contraindicated for persons with high blood pressure, cardiac disorders, diabetes, ulcers, epilepsy, and other disorders.  2."
