    "fullText": "66. Guava (*Psidium guajava*) - **Famille Botanique** :  - **Noms Usuels / Synonymes** : Guava - **Parties Utilisées** : Fruit, leaf, bark - **Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme** : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - **Source Primaire Rain-Tree** : [Guava Monograph on Rain-Tree. com](https://www. rain-tree. com/guava. htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Guava is rich in tannins  - phenols  - triterpenes  - flavonoids  - essential oils  - saponins  - carotenoids  - lectins - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - corn  - squash  - and other cultivated plants  - In fact  - and Indians also employ it for sore throats  - vomiting - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1.  **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : 1.  Guava has recently demonstrated cardiac depressant activity and should be used with caution by those on heart medications.  2.  Guava fruit has shown to lower blood sugar levels and it should be avoided by people with hypoglycemia.  2."
