    "fullText": "67. Guayusa (*Ilex guayusa*) - **Famille Botanique** :  - **Noms Usuels / Synonymes** : Guayusa - **Parties Utilisées** : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - **Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme** : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - **Source Primaire Rain-Tree** : [Guayusa Monograph on Rain-Tree. com](https://www. rain-tree. com/guayusa. htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Guayusa has a similar chemical makeup of its closely related “cousin  - ” yerba mate  - Both are significant sources of caffeine  - with guayusa providing a bit more  - Guayusa leaves contain 1  - 73–3  - 48% caffeine (compared to 0  - 7–2% in yerba mate and 1–2 - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - ulcers  - heart diseases  - and other diseases  - Guayusa might lower blood sugar levels  - anxiety  - fast heart rate  - and more - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1."
