    "fullText": "70. Huacapu (*Minquartia guianensis*) - **Famille Botanique** :  - **Noms Usuels / Synonymes** : Huacapu - **Parties Utilisées** : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - **Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme** : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - **Source Primaire Rain-Tree** : [Huacapu Monograph on Rain-Tree. com](https://www. rain-tree. com/huacapu. htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Huacapu bark contains triterpenes  - xanthones  - lipids  - tannins  - and acids  - The main bioactive chemical in the bark is a lipid called minquartynoic acid  - ovarian  - colon and neuroblastoma cancer cell lines - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - The bark is also often used as a malaria remedy  - as well as for tuberculosis  - hepatitis  - and rheumatism by various Indian communities in the Amazon  - more often  - the inner bark is used when preparing remedies for humans - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1."
