    "excerpt": "**Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : Likewise, there has been little clinical research on iporuru - despite its long history of use in South American herbal medicine.  That which has been done, however, does help explain some of its traditional uses.  Pharmacognosy students in Sweden documented that an ethano...",
    "fullText": "72. Iporuru (*Alchornea castaneifolia*) **Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : Likewise, there has been little clinical research on iporuru - despite its long history of use in South American herbal medicine.  That which has been done, however, does help explain some of its traditional uses.  Pharmacognosy students in Sweden documented that an ethanol extract of the stembark was capable of reducing lab-induced swelling and inflammation in rats when applied topically.  These res...  3.  **Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel** : For centuries the indigenous peoples of the Amazon have used the bark and leaves of iporuru for many different purposes and prepared it in many different ways.  The plant commonly is used with other plants during shamanistic training and, sometimes, is an ingredient in ayahuasca (a hallucinogenic, multi-herb decoction used by South American shamans)..."
