    "fullText": "73. Jaborandi (*Pilocarpus jaborandi*) An overdose may cause such symptoms as flushing, profuse sweating and salivation, urinary frequency, nausea, rapid pulse, contracted pupils, diarrhea or fatal pulmonary edema.  3.  The plant may induce bradycardia.  Those with cardiac or circulatory conditions should not take jaborandi.  4.  Jaborandi may induce dehydration due to excessive perspiration and urination.  If using jaborandi, electrolyte and fluid status must be monitored and maintained.  2.  **Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : There are well over a thousand clinical studies published on pilocarpine.  As with most plant-based drugs, however, the use of the whole natural plant fell out of use as a natural remedy (and failed to attract further research efforts) in favor of the single isolated active ingredient that was turned into a prescription drug.  The PDR for Herbal Medicines indicates that the effects of jaborandi leav...  3."
