    "fullText": "73. Jaborandi (*Pilocarpus jaborandi*) **Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel** : In 1570, Gabriel Soares de Souza, a European observer, first recorded that the Guarani Indians of Brazil were using jaborandi to treat mouth ulcers.  In the 1630's two Dutch West Indian Company scientists documented other Brazilian Indians using it as a tonic or panacea for colds and flu, a remedy against gonorrhea and kidney stones and found that i...  - **Posologie & Modes d'Administration** :  - **Dosage Standard** : reduces glacoma reduces inflammation Leaves promotes perspiration increases milk flow Not recommended increases saliva increases urination increases heart rate  - **Infusion / Décoction** : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.   - **Teinture** : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour.  - **Contre-indications & Précautions** :  - 1.  Pilocarpine has shown to increase the rate of birth defects in animal studies."
