    "fullText": "73. Jaborandi (*Pilocarpus jaborandi*) Jaborandi should not be taken during pregnancy or while breastfeeding.  2.  Both jaborandi and pilocarpine may cause headaches and can irritate the stomach and cause vomiting and nausea.  An overdose may cause such symptoms as flushing, profuse sweating and salivation, urinary frequency, nausea, rapid pulse, contracted pupils, diarrhea or fatal pulmonary edema.  3.  The plant may induce bradycardia.  Those with cardiac or circulatory conditions should not take jaborandi.  4.  Jaborandi may induce dehydration due to excessive perspiration and urination.  If using jaborandi, electrolyte and fluid status must be monitored and maintained.  - **Note Vitaliste** : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr.  Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne."
