    "fullText": "80. Jurubeba (*Solanum paniculatum*) - **Famille Botanique** :  - **Noms Usuels / Synonymes** : Jurubeba - **Parties Utilisées** : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - **Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme** : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - **Source Primaire Rain-Tree** : [Jurubeba Monograph on Rain-Tree. com](https://www. rain-tree. com/jurubeba. htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Jurubeba's active constituents were first documented in the 1960s  - when German researchers discovered novel plant steroids  - saponins  - glycosides  - and alkaloids in the root  - stem  - and leaves  - The alkaloids were found more abundantly in the root - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - Those with cardiovascular disorders  - hypotension  - Do not use chronically (daily) for longer than 30 days - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1.  **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : 1."
