    "excerpt": "People with blood disorders such as hemophilia, those taking heart medications or blood thinners, or those with other heart problems such as low blood pressure should not use this plant without supervision and advice of a qualified health care practitioner.  Animal studies report that mullaca can lower blood glucose le...",
    "fullText": "89. Mullaca (*Physalis angulata*) People with blood disorders such as hemophilia, those taking heart medications or blood thinners, or those with other heart problems such as low blood pressure should not use this plant without supervision and advice of a qualified health care practitioner.  Animal studies report that mullaca can lower blood glucose levels.  Diabetics should use with caution and test their glucose levels regularly until they determine what effects mullaca might have on their glucose levels as diabetic medications may need adjusting.  - **Note Vitaliste** : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr.  Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne."
