    "excerpt": "Mulungu has long been used in Brazil by indigenous peoples as a natural sedative: it has been used to calm an overexcited nervous system and promote a restful sleep.  In both North and South American herbal medicine systems mulun...  - **Posologie & Modes d'Administration** :  - **Dosage Standard** : relieves pain kill...",
    "fullText": "90. Mulungu (*Erythrina mulungu*) Mulungu has long been used in Brazil by indigenous peoples as a natural sedative: it has been used to calm an overexcited nervous system and promote a restful sleep.  In both North and South American herbal medicine systems mulun...  - **Posologie & Modes d'Administration** :  - **Dosage Standard** : relieves pain kills bacteria Bark, root reduces anxiety Decoction: 1/2 cup 1-2 calms nerves times daily moderately sedative Tincture: 1-2 ml twice daily supports liver reduces blood pressure regulates heart beat  - **Infusion / Décoction** : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.   - **Teinture** : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour.  - **Contre-indications & Précautions** :  - 1.  This plant is a sedative and may cause drowsiness.  2.  In traditional medicine the plant is used to lower blood pressure.  Clinical research with animals has documented hypotensive actions."
