    "fullText": "92. Mutamba (*Guazuma ulmifolia*) - **Famille Botanique** : Sterculiaceae - **Noms Usuels / Synonymes** : Mutamba - **Parties Utilisées** : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - **Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme** : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - **Source Primaire Rain-Tree** : [Mutamba Monograph on Rain-Tree. com](https://www. rain-tree. com/mutamba. htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - One in particular  - procyanidin B-2  - In 1999  - From 2000 to 2002  - The leaves of mutamba contain caffeine  - however none has been found in the bark of the tree  - Mutamba's main plant chemicals include: caryophyllene  - catechins - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - People with a history of heart problems  - those taking heart medications - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1.  **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : 1.  Mutamba bark has been documented in several animal studies to have uterine stimulant activity and it should not be taken during pregnancy.  2."
