    "fullText": "97. Pau d'Arco (*Tabebuia impetiginosa*) **Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : Over many years pau d’arco has continued to demonstrate anti-tumorous, anti-cancer and anti-leukemic actions in many types of cancer at low dosages without toxicity to healthy cells.  These included breast carcinoma, lung carcinoma, cervical carcinoma, and liver carcinomas with the GI50 values (corresponding to a sample concentration achieving 50% growth inhibition in human tumor cell lines) report...  3.  **Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel** : Pau d'arco has a long and well-documented history of use by the indigenous peoples of the rainforest.  Indications imply that its use may actually predate the Incas.  Throughout South America, tribes living thousands of miles apart have employed it for the same medicinal purposes for hundreds of years.  Several Indian tribes of the rainforest have use..."
