    "fullText": "98. Pedra Hume Caa (*Myrcia salicifolia*) - **Famille Botanique** :  - **Noms Usuels / Synonymes** : Pedra hume ca&aacute, pedra-ume-ca&aacute, insulina vegetal - **Parties Utilisées** : Leaves - **Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme** : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - **Source Primaire Rain-Tree** : [Pedra Hume Caa Monograph on Rain-Tree. com](https://www. rain-tree. com/pedra. htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Phytochemical analysis of pedra hume caá reveals a high content of flavonoids  - flavonols  - and flavanones  - In 1998  - These new flavanone glucosides were named myrciacitrins I and II  - the new acetophenone glucosides were named myrciaphenones A and B  - and thus protect the nerves  - For this reason - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - It is contraindicated in those with hypoglycemia - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1.  **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : 1.  Pedra hume caá has been documented to lower blood sugar levels in animal and human studies."
