    "fullText": "101. Piri-piri (*Cyperus articulatus*) - **Famille Botanique** :  - **Noms Usuels / Synonymes** : Piri-piri - **Parties Utilisées** : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - **Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme** : Immunité & Anti-infectieux (Immunomodulateur & Antiviral) - **Source Primaire Rain-Tree** : [Piri-piri Monograph on Rain-Tree. com](https://www. rain-tree. com/piri-piri. htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Piri-piri contains flavonoids  - polyphenols  - saponins  - tannins  - terpenes and sugars  - Two of these chemicals  - called cyperotundone and alpha-cyperone  - have been reported with antimalarial actions - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - The tall stems and/or the rhizomes are dried and powdered  - to facilitate child birth or to induce an abortion  - as a contraceptive  - and for throat cancer  - and used externally to heal wounds and treat snake bite  - and to allay fright and nervousness - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1."
