    "excerpt": "Hibiscus flowers are a natural source of iron and have been used to treat anemia in some countries with mixed results.  If you have hemochromatosis (high iron levels), you should avoid using this remedy.  2.  **Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : The first area of research on roselle is one of the most documen...",
    "fullText": "106. Roselle (* *) Hibiscus flowers are a natural source of iron and have been used to treat anemia in some countries with mixed results.  If you have hemochromatosis (high iron levels), you should avoid using this remedy.  2.  **Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : The first area of research on roselle is one of the most documented and verified – the antioxidant action of roselle calyces.  Substances called free radicals and reactive oxygen species (ROS) are a product of normal life, created by metabolizing foods, and by various other chemical interactions in our bodies which are quite normal.  The human body has a natural built-in antioxidant system that prod...  3.  **Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel** : All parts of the roselle shrub have been used medicinally around the world: leaves, flower calyces, seeds, and seed oil.  This book will focus on the uses of the roselle’s flower calyces."
