    "fullText": "106. Roselle (* *) The rule of thumb in most traditional medicine systems is to prepare a decoction (boiling in water for 10 minutes) if you’re using dried flower calyces and to prep...  - **Posologie & Modes d'Administration** :  - **Dosage Standard** : lowers blood pressure slows ageing Flower calyces lowers cholesterol reduces weight Decocotion: 1 cup 1-2 times daily prevents heart disease kills bacteria Capsules: 1-2 g twice daily fights free radicals kills fungi unclogs arteries kills viruses reduces inflammation protects skin protects heart prevents kidney stones increases urination protects liver lowers blood sugar protects brain enhances memory reduces diabetic complications  - **Infusion / Décoction** : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.   - **Teinture** : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour.  - **Contre-indications & Précautions** :  - 1.  Do not use hibiscus flowers while breastfeeding."
