    "fullText": "110. Sarsaparilla (*Smilax officinalis*) - **Famille Botanique** : Smilacaceae - **Noms Usuels / Synonymes** : Sarsaparilla, salsaparrilha, khao yen, saparna, smilace, smilax, zarzaparilla, jupicanga - **Parties Utilisées** : Root - **Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme** : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - **Source Primaire Rain-Tree** : [Sarsaparilla Monograph on Rain-Tree. com](https://www. rain-tree. com/sarsaparilla. htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Sarsaparilla contains the plant steroids sarsasapogenin  - smilagenin  - sitosterol  - stigmasterol  - and pollinastanol  - and the saponins sarsasaponin  - smilasaponin  - sarsaparilloside - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - rheumatism  - skin ailments  - and as a general tonic for physical weakness  - and against the common cold  - armadillos are \"on the menu\" in indigenous diets)  - European physicians considered sarsaparilla root a tonic - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1."
