    "fullText": "117. Ubos (*Spondias mombin*) - **Famille Botanique** :  - **Noms Usuels / Synonymes** : Ubos - **Parties Utilisées** : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - **Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme** : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - **Source Primaire Rain-Tree** : [Ubos Monograph on Rain-Tree. com](https://www. rain-tree. com/ubos. htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Ubos leaves and bark contains tannins  - saponins  - flavonoids  - sterols  - quinones  - and antioxidant chemicals  - This natural plant chemical has been reported with antibacterial  - antiviral - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - Ubos bark is traditionally used as a contraceptive  - Ubos leaves contains salicylic acid derivatives  - If allergic or sensitive to aspirin or salicylic acid  - avoid use of the leaves  - Drug Interactions: None reported  - Worldwide Ethnomedical Uses Africa for bleeding  - childbirth  - chronic diarrhea - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1."
