    "fullText": "117. Ubos (*Spondias mombin*) displays an anti-inflammatory effect and suppresses inducible formation of tumor necrosis factor-a and nitric oxide (NO). \" J.  Immunotoxicol.  2011 Jan-Mar; 8(1): 10-6.  Abad, M. , et al.  \"Antiinflammatory activity of some medicinal plant extracts from Venezuela. \" J.  Ethnopharmacol.  1996; 55: 63-68.  Calderon, A. , et al.  \"Forest plot as a tool to demonstrate the pharmaceutical potential of plants in a tropical forest of Panama. \" Econ.  Bot.  2000; 54(3): 278-294.  Abad, M. , et al.  \"Anti-inflammatory activity of some medicinal plant extracts from Venezuela. \" J.  Ethnopharmacol.  1996; 55(1): 63-68.  Antimicrobial Actions (bacteria, virus, fungi, candida): Ubos bark has been reported with antibacterial actions in test tube studies against Pseudomonas aeruginosa and Bacillus cereus.  It was also reported to inhibit human rotovirus by 82% in vitro which might explain its long standing use for diarrhea."
