    "excerpt": "**Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : 1.  The seed may cause birth defects and has uterine stimulant activity.  It should not be used during pregnancy.  2.  Velvet bean has shown to lower blood sugar.  Those with hypoglycemia or diabetes should only use Velvet bean under the supervision of a qualified healthcare practi...",
    "fullText": "120. Velvet Bean (*Mucuna pruriens*) **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : 1.  The seed may cause birth defects and has uterine stimulant activity.  It should not be used during pregnancy.  2.  Velvet bean has shown to lower blood sugar.  Those with hypoglycemia or diabetes should only use Velvet bean under the supervision of a qualified healthcare practitioner.  3.  Velvet bean is contraindicated in combination with M. A. O.  inhibitors.  4.  Velvet bean has androgenic activity, increasing testosterone levels.  Persons with excessive androgen syndromes should avoid using Velvet bean.  5.  Velvet bean inhibits prolactin.  If you have a medical condition resulting in inadequate levels of prolactin in the body, do not use Velvet bean unless under the direction or your healthcare practitioner.  6.  The seed contains high quantities of L-dopa.  Levodopa is the pharmaceutical medication used for Parkinson's disease."
