    "fullText": "122. Ayapana (Eupatorium ayapana) in the Tropical Plant Database of herbal remedies (*Eupatorium triplinerve*) htm) - **Principes Phytochimiques Actifs** :  - Ayapana is a rich source of naturally occurring coumarin chemicals  - Coumarin has clinical value as the precursor for several anticoagulant drugs  - most notably  - one widely prescribed drug called warfarin  - Ayapana also contains a natural coumarin chemical named ayapanin  - herniarin  - gerniarin  - and methylumbelliferone - **Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques** :  - stomach pain  - swellings  - and as a overall detoxifier  - For internal hemorrhages  - cicatrizant (closes wounds)  - astringent (dries secretions) - **Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor)** : 1.  **Actions Principales (Rain-Tree)** : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs.  2.  **Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : Researchers around the world have studied ayapana."
