    "fullText": "122. Ayapana (Eupatorium ayapana) in the Tropical Plant Database of herbal remedies (*Eupatorium triplinerve*) - **Posologie & Modes d'Administration** :  - **Dosage Standard** : eases nausea antiseptic leaves calms coughs promotes healing Infusion: 1 cup twice daily reduces inflammation kills cancer cells stops bleeding detoxifies protects cells and organs reduces fever relieves pain softens skin heals wounds kills bacteria aids digestion kills fungi fights free radicals relieves oxidative stress prevents ulcers  - **Infusion / Décoction** : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.   - **Teinture** : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour.  - **Contre-indications & Précautions** :  - Ayapana leaves contain naturally occurring coumarins.  Coumarin has an anti-coagulant and blood thinning effect and is a precursor to coumadin drugs.  Consult with your physician before taking this plant if you are taking coumadin drugs or if coumadin anticoagulant type drugs are contraindicated for your condition."
