    "fullText": "124. YERBA MATE (Ilex paraguariensis) Database file in the Tropical Plant Database (*Ilex paraguayiensis*) More than 50 human, animal and test tube studies reveal how yerba mate can reduce or prevent unstable molecules (called free radicals or reactive oxygen species) from harming various cells and organs in the body (called oxidative stress).  The damage caused by oxidative stress can be a ...  3.  **Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel** : Yerba mate was has been used as a beverage since the time of the ancient Indians of Brazil and Paraguay.  In the early 16th century, Juan de Solís, a Spanish explorer of South America's famed La Plata River, reported that the Guarani Indians of Paraguay brewed a leaf tea that \"produced exhilaration and relief from fatigue. \" The Spaniards tried the b..."
