    "fullText": "126. Yacon (Smallanthus sonchifolius) Database file in the Tropical Plant Database for herbal remedies (*Smallanthus sonchifolius*) **Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique** : Yacon root contains a high concentration of substances called fructooligosaccharides (FOS) and inulin, which are types of prebiotic soluble fibers.  FOS are not digested in the upper gastrointestinal tract, so they don’t spike blood glucose levels.  They reach the colon intact and feed specific beneficial gut bacteria which improves insulin sensitivity.  Several species of bacteria are responsible fo...  3.  **Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel** : In early evolutionary periods, Andean farmers had already recognized the value of yacon as a cultivated food crop.  Yacon has been discovered in burial grounds from centuries before the Incas.  The first written record of yacon was in 1615 when Felipe Guaman Poma de Ayala included it in a list of 55 native crops cultivated by the Andeans.  In South Am..."
