    "fullText": "126. Yacon (Smallanthus sonchifolius) Database file in the Tropical Plant Database for herbal remedies (*Smallanthus sonchifolius*) - **Posologie & Modes d'Administration** :  - **Dosage Standard** : lowers blood sugar kills bacteria Root fights free radicals kills fungi Powder or Syrup relieves oxidative stress lowers cholesterol follow labeled instructions feeds friendly gut bacteria lowers triglycerides protect brain protects organs protect digestive tract relieves depression promotes weight loss prevents chronic diseases  - **Infusion / Décoction** : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.   - **Teinture** : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour.  - **Contre-indications & Précautions** :  - The leaves have demonstrated the ability to significantly lower blood sugar levels.  Diabetics should check with a practitioner before using the leaves and monitor their blood sugar levels accordingly as medications may need adjustment.  Overconsumption of the root can lead to bloating, gas, or diarrhea due to its high FOS content."
